      "name": "D13",
      "label": "GPIO13 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "D13",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high",
        "spi_ss"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED — onboard LED1, active-high, standard series-resistor-to-GND circuit (RP2040 GPIO13 -> R8 330ohm -> LED1 -> GND). Confirmed via ArtronShop's official schematic PDF (dl.artronshop.co.th/RP2-Nano/RP2 Nano schematic.pdf, REV 1.0, 23/7/2022). This GPIO is also broken out to the Nano header as D13/CS (PIN_SPI1_SS / global SS), genuinely and fully wired per ArtronShop's own pinout diagram (D10=SCK, D11=MOSI, D12=MISO, D13=CS all labelled SPI) — mirroring the classic Arduino Uno/Nano D13 LED+SPI dual-purpose tradition, so the bus is not spare and the auto-appended SS capability is left as-is (not a contamination bug like adafruit_feather_scorpio's vendor-unused PIN_SPI0_SS). digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins; pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming."
    },
